{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul","id":1368475,"title":"Artifact \u2022\u2022 goremaul","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-17T00:18:35-08:00","id":1368475,"title":"Artifact \u2022\u2022 goremaul","content":"One of my players bought the Artifact \u2022\u2022 merit, and wants it to be his weapon. Yes, Artifact 2, not three. I'm thinking, for a power of &quot;limited but still supernatural usefulness,&quot; the hammer adds [Essence] dice to resist knockdown. Does that seem about right for Artifact \u2022\u2022?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T00:24:55-08:00","id":1368476,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't give Artifact statline, but a small bonus along the lines of other \u2022\u2022ers that happens to be stapled to a mace seems fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T00:38:20-08:00","id":1368479,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there are no canonical Artifact oo weapons. Each one is a weapon of legend capable of awakening Evocations and is thus at least Artifact ooo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T00:43:03-08:00","id":1368481,"title":"","content":"What the others noted. The game itself notes that the minimum is Artifact OOO for weapons. To be blunt, if that player were at my table, I'd tell the player &quot;Look the rules say that artifact weapons take 3 Merit Dots. We'll design a different artifact, but you're not getting a Goremaul at Art 2&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T01:19:19-08:00","id":1368486,"title":"","content":"Note too that &quot;Artifact weapon statline without Evocations&quot; Is kind of not a fair balancing argument etiher since even the guys who took the one with a minor attunement power or whatever paid the three dots.<br /> <br /> I can see an Artifact 2 weapon. It just would be using mundane weapon stats, not artifact, and not have any potential besides a minor bonus or something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T03:43:52-08:00","id":1368506,"title":"","content":"The Traveller's Staff is Artifact 2, page 601.<br /> <br /> It uses the traits of a mundane weapon.<br /> <br /> You can absolutely have an artifact hammer at two dots. But it's not a Goremaul and won't have artifact weapon traits.<br /> <br /> How would Essence dice to resist knockdown work? Roll Essence and not get knocked down on a success? That'd be fine on an Artifact 2 with mundane hammer stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T17:59:35-08:00","id":1368653,"title":"","content":"Pick a neat \u25cf\u25cf hearthstone and make it a hammer instead of a rock, problem solved. <br /> <br /> Don't give it artifact stats. Keep it mundane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T22:00:38-08:00","id":1368682,"title":"","content":"I agree that a weapon could have mundane stats and some minor benefit for Artifact 2. But the player should probably be reminded that spending one more point in the Artifact merit would have a huge marginal benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T02:30:07-08:00","id":1369116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1368653#post1368653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pick a neat \u25cf\u25cf hearthstone and make it a hammer instead of a rock, problem solved. <br /> <br /> Don't give it artifact stats. Keep it mundane.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you still have a better effect than a two-dot Hearthstone alone, since it's a weapon as well. Maybe if it was a one-dot Hearthstone, sure. <br /> <br /> For a two-dot weapon, I'd probably make it a mundane item with a Hearthstone slot instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T04:54:40-08:00","id":1369123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369116#post1369116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you still have a better effect than a two-dot Hearthstone alone, since it's a weapon as well. Maybe if it was a one-dot Hearthstone, sure.<br /> <br /> For a two-dot weapon, I'd probably make it a mundane item with a Hearthstone slot instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>A mundane weapon ain't really worth anything in terms of Merit dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T07:05:01-08:00","id":1369126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369123#post1369123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mundane weapon ain't really worth anything in terms of Merit dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>But a Hearthstone Amulet is a two dot Artifact in and of itself. An amulet which is also a weapon AND the Hearthstone itself is basically 4 dots of Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T07:15:06-08:00","id":1369127,"title":"","content":"Is it though? Really?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T11:12:07-08:00","id":1369160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369126#post1369126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But a Hearthstone Amulet is a two dot Artifact in and of itself. An amulet which is also a weapon AND the Hearthstone itself is basically 4 dots of Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me unpack this a bit.<br /> <br /> Hearthstones require a socket (such as one in the Amulet) to grant Essence regeneration, and <i>most,</i> but definitely not <i>all</i> of them need to be socketed to access their other effects.<br /> <br /> Pretty sure Sorcerous didn't mean to suggest the hammer should regenerate Essence like a Hearthstone, just have a power comparable to a two-dot one slapped on a mundane hammer statblock.<br /> <br /> I think that's not gonna upset the balance compared to the Hearthstone that's not also a hammer, but can still be socketed on the flipside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T12:08:32-08:00","id":1369172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369116#post1369116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you still have a better effect than a two-dot Hearthstone alone, since it's a weapon as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The upside is your mace is also a hearthstone. The downside is have you ever tried to socket a mace in your artifact whatever's heartstone socket?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","user":"vwllss trnt prncss","date":". 02-20-2020, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T12:26:22-08:00","id":1369174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369160#post1369160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me unpack this a bit.<br /> <br /> Hearthstones require a socket (such as one in the Amulet) to grant Essence regeneration, and <i>most,</i> but definitely not <i>all</i> of them need to be socketed to access their other effects.<br /> <br /> Pretty sure Sorcerous didn't mean to suggest the hammer should regenerate Essence like a Hearthstone, just have a power comparable to a two-dot one slapped on a mundane hammer statblock.<br /> <br /> I think that's not gonna upset the balance compared to the Hearthstone that's not also a hammer, but can still be socketed on the flipside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aha! That makes more sense. That would work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T12:39:52-08:00","id":1369177,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that'd be broadly equivalent to a Traveller's Staff or a an Ultimately Useful Tube.<br /> <br /> Mundane hammer traits and a minor power based on a standard hearthstone is solidly Artifact 2. (Provided that the hammer itself is NOT a Hearthstone.)<br /> <br /> Some cool Hearthstones for inspiration for the powers a magical hammer might have are: Stone of the Ram's Horn; Iron Soul Stone; Root-of-the-Earth Gemstone; Gemstone of Shattering Force; or Stone of the Emerald Rooster.<br /> <br /> Good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T23:53:12-08:00","id":1369287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369172#post1369172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The upside is your mace is also a hearthstone. The downside is have you ever tried to socket a mace in your artifact whatever's heartstone socket?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sledge Stone: socketed weapon gains -5 Accuracy, but everything hit by it is also hit by a mundane sledgehammer (automatically successful attack with zero extra successes, counts user's Strength to damage normally). Socketed armor grants -5 Mobility penalty, but everyone who enters into close range with you (whether by your movement or theirs) takes an automatic hit from a sledgehammer (Withering only, automatic hit with zero extra successes, does not count user's Strength to damage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T00:01:57-08:00","id":1369290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369287#post1369287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sledge Stone: socketed weapon gains -5 Accuracy, but everything hit by it is also hit by a mundane sledgehammer (automatically successful attack with zero extra successes, counts user's Strength to damage normally). Socketed armor grants -5 Mobility penalty, but everyone who enters into close range with you (whether by your movement or theirs) takes an automatic hit from a sledgehammer (Withering only, automatic hit with zero extra successes, does not count user's Strength to damage).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take three! Four if you give me a discount on that hearthstone amulet. <br /> GO GO ARMORED SCOUT'S INVIGORATION! FORM OF: BALL OF HAMMERS!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T00:28:32-08:00","id":1369295,"title":"","content":"If the player is taking an Artifact 2 hammer, then they aren't taking an Artifact 3 or 4 or 5 weapon. and yeah, those costs more bonus points, but honest to god of all the things uneven about exalted, Bonus Points is 3 legged table on a trampoline on the Titanic (for 2 dots you can get a horse. for 3 dots you can get a t-rex). It's not an issue to just make a 2 dot hearthstone into a weapon itself, considering the power spike of 3 dot artifacts comparatively. <br /> <br /> Martial Arts equals a T-Rex and one of Odin's Ravens. Stormcaller equals having access to a creation-spanning network of agents. There's a<b> <i>first age battleship</i> </b>that costs less than artifact heavy armor for one person. Learning a few languages costs as much as being rich as a literal king. Getting a what amounts to a free socket on a mundane weapon isn't going to unbalance anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T04:20:45-08:00","id":1369325,"title":"","content":"Another thing is, while it's true that Artifact weapons are intended to be treated as these unique, storied pieces, and thus begin at three dots of Artifact Merit, those three dots grant you something more than just an artifact weapon statline. You get the potential of unlocking Evocations, and every weapon written up in core or Arms either comes with a first Evocation unlocked or has some bonus above the basic stats. <br /> <br /> Considering that, from a purely mechanical perspective, a case can be made for making a two-dot Goremaul that only comes with the basic statline, no unique bonuses, no Hearthstone socket and no Evocation potential. Again, I'm not saying it'd be a particularly great Artifact, and it's definitely against the intent of the third edition, but if one didn't care about those considerations, I don't think it'd be particularly unbalanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T04:38:46-08:00","id":1369330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369177#post1369177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that'd be broadly equivalent to a Traveller's Staff or a an Ultimately Useful Tube.<br /> <br /> Mundane hammer traits and a minor power based on a standard hearthstone is solidly Artifact 2. (Provided that the hammer itself is NOT a Hearthstone.)<br /> <br /> Some cool Hearthstones for inspiration for the powers a magical hammer might have are: Stone of the Ram's Horn; Iron Soul Stone; Root-of-the-Earth Gemstone; Gemstone of Shattering Force; or Stone of the Emerald Rooster.<br /> <br /> Good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I took this option. I gave him the Hammer of Shattering Force, with the stats of a mundane two-handed sledge and the power of a Gemstone of Shattering Force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T05:43:56-08:00","id":1369341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369325#post1369325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing is, while it's true that Artifact weapons are intended to be treated as these unique, storied pieces, and thus begin at three dots of Artifact Merit, those three dots grant you something more than just an artifact weapon statline. You get the potential of unlocking Evocations, and every weapon written up in core or Arms either comes with a first Evocation unlocked or has some bonus above the basic stats. <br /> <br /> Considering that, from a purely mechanical perspective, a case can be made for making a two-dot Goremaul that only comes with the basic statline, no unique bonuses, no Hearthstone socket and no Evocation potential. Again, I'm not saying it'd be a particularly great Artifact, and it's definitely against the intent of the third edition, but if one didn't care about those considerations, I don't think it'd be particularly unbalanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>What\u2019s the difference between a 2-dot artifact weapon with no Evocation potential, and a 3-dot artifact weapon for which you never take an Evocation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T05:59:27-08:00","id":1369347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369341#post1369341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s the difference between a 2-dot artifact weapon with no Evocation potential, and a 3-dot artifact weapon for which you never take an Evocation?</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the difference between a 3-dot artifact weapon and a 5-dot artifact weapon if you never take Evocations for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1