 horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T06:38:30-08:00","id":1369354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369351#post1369351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably the attunemnet bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is part of the Evocations potential, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T10:06:40-08:00","id":1369398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369354#post1369354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is part of the Evocations potential, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd disagree, since an attunement bonus is free. More to the point, the statline alone is worth the 3 dots. I do not know why you'd spend 5 dots on an artifact and not buy evocations (again, the attunement bonus is the only innate way you see a powerup).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T10:27:34-08:00","id":1369400,"title":"","content":"A broken 3-dot Goremaul that's currently a particularly ornate looking sledgehammer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T11:41:59-08:00","id":1369413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369400#post1369400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A broken 3-dot Goremaul that's currently a particularly ornate looking sledgehammer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also a good idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369295#post1369295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the player is taking an Artifact 2 hammer, then they aren't taking an Artifact 3 or 4 or 5 weapon. and yeah, those costs more bonus points, but honest to god of all the things uneven about exalted, Bonus Points is 3 legged table on a trampoline on the Titanic (for 2 dots you can get a horse. for 3 dots you can get a t-rex). It's not an issue to just make a 2 dot hearthstone into a weapon itself, considering the power spike of 3 dot artifacts comparatively. <br /> <br /> Martial Arts equals a T-Rex and one of Odin's Ravens. Stormcaller equals having access to a creation-spanning network of agents. There's a<b> <i>first age battleship</i> </b>that costs less than artifact heavy armor for one person. Learning a few languages costs as much as being rich as a literal king. Getting a what amounts to a free socket on a mundane weapon isn't going to unbalance anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strongly disagree.<br /> <br /> If the system is unbalanced; the solution isn't to ignore the advice on how to balance it and make it more unbalanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-21-2020, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T19:39:15-08:00","id":1369491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369413#post1369413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also a good idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> Strongly disagree.<br /> <br /> If the system is unbalanced; the solution isn't to ignore the advice on how to balance it and make it more unbalanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you mean, but we are in a position where you are arguing that Hakkonen's player should be forced to get more power than they asked for, for the sake of game balance. The player wants a little power at a small cost, but instead you think they should be forced to spend a single bp more and get a massive boost in power- namely artifact statlines and the potential for evocations. <br /> <br /> It might be a table difference, but if a player asked me to let them have a little cool thing at a fairly low cost in line with other little cool things, yeah. I'd allow it. I'm not gonna tell a player they can't have a 2 dot Millenium Falcon and instead have to buy a 3 dot Star Destroyer. <br /> <br /> I do see what you mean though. It is technically an advantage of having a 2 dot hearthstone without worrying about sockets, but putting on my Doyalist Game Dev hat i just don't see how that incredibly niche change is going to effect a player's experience at the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T23:10:25-08:00","id":1369515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369398#post1369398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd disagree, since an attunement bonus is free.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, it's not free - it's what you pay those dots for! Volcano Cutter's attunement bonus is stronger than Adorei's because you pay more dots for the former.<br /> Second, it most definitely is a part of the weapons Evocations, as evidenced by fact that it's described under the headline that reads &quot;Evocations of (Artifact name)&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More to the point, the statline alone is worth the 3 dots. </div> </div> </div>And I don't think I agree with it. Nor do I see the system agrees, seeing how it gives you that attunement bonus on top.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not know why you'd spend 5 dots on an artifact and not buy evocations (again, the attunement bonus is the only innate way you see a powerup). </div> </div> </div>I do not know why you'd spend three dots on an artifact and not buy evocations*. Which is why I'm arguing that yes, those potential Evocations are a large part of what you're paying for when you buy an artifact rated 3 dots or higher.<br /> <br /> *Obviously, if you only care about the artifact weapon statline, it makes more sense to buy a 3-dots daiklave than a 5-dots one. This doesn't change the fact that by not pursuing Evocations at all, you're wasting part of what you paid for with your Merit dots - you just waste even more with greater weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":582,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","user":"Morangias","date":". 02-22-2020, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T23:26:29-08:00","id":1369519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369515#post1369515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don't think I agree with it. Nor do I see the system agrees, seeing how it gives you that attunement bonus on top.</div> </div> </div> </div>But <i>not all</i> of them have an attunement bonus for all users. Some only unlock when (or if) you do a certain thing; some only unlock for free if you\u2019re Resonant. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369515#post1369515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not know why you'd spend three dots on an artifact and not buy evocations*.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I may not <i>want to</i>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369515#post1369515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why I'm arguing that yes, those potential Evocations are a large part of what you're paying for when you buy an artifact rated 3 dots or higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet we have no examples of an artifact 2 with artifact weapon stats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369515#post1369515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't change the fact that by not pursuing Evocations at all, you're wasting part of what you paid for with your Merit dots\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>What\u2019s the difference between a character who doesn\u2019t pursue Evocations because he is only interested in the artifact stats, and a character who doesn\u2019t pursue Evocations because he\u2019s <i>already buying</i> Martial Arts Charms or sorcery spells or Eclipse Charms with his Solar XP, and doesn\u2019t want to hinder his progression with one more thing on the pile (but still wants to hit as hard with his sword as his circle-mates)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-22-2020, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T00:31:24-08:00","id":1369527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369491#post1369491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get what you mean, but we are in a position where you are arguing that Hakkonen's player should be forced to get more power than they asked for, for the sake of game balance. The player wants a little power at a small cost, but instead you think they should be forced to spend a single bp more and get a massive boost in power- namely artifact statlines and the potential for evocations. <br /> <br /> It might be a table difference, but if a player asked me to let them have a little cool thing at a fairly low cost in line with other little cool things, yeah. I'd allow it. I'm not gonna tell a player they can't have a 2 dot Millenium Falcon and instead have to buy a 3 dot Star Destroyer. <br /> <br /> I do see what you mean though. It is technically an advantage of having a 2 dot hearthstone without worrying about sockets, but putting on my Doyalist Game Dev hat i just don't see how that incredibly niche change is going to effect a player's experience at the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm happy for them to have a two dot Artifact. A Traveller's Staff is a two dot Artifact.<br /> <br /> A mundane weapon with a minor power is absolutely fine.<br /> <br /> I'm not happy with them getting a 3 dot Artifact for 2 dots, or a two dot Hearthstone AND a two dot Artifact for only two dots.<br /> <br /> They absolutely can have a two dot Falcon. But you can't say &quot;oh it's only a Victory Class Star Destroyer have it for two dots&quot; or &quot;The Falcon and Luke's X-wing aren't as good as a Star Destroyer so have the X-wing for free&quot;.<br /> <br /> If they player wants the Falcon and buys the Falcon they should get the Falcon.<br /> <br /> OP's actual solution to this is a really good one which I support.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-22-2020, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T01:22:28-08:00","id":1369530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369519#post1369519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet we have no examples of an artifact 2 with artifact weapon stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I acknowledged that in the very beginning. What I'm arguing is that this is due to a thematic choice of having each artifact weapon and armor a unique relic with unique magical powers, and not due to the overwhelming power of the artifact weapon/armor stats themselves, and that if one were to willfully and knowingly ignore that thematic restriction and allow an artifact whose sole power is having artifact weapon stats, it wouldn't be strong enough to merit a 3-dots cost, and thus would be more fairly priced as a 2-dot artifact.<br /> <br /> Which, again, I'm not saying everyone should allow such an item in their games. I'm all for Daiklaves being unique Zanpakutos. But there are different people, different campaigns and different tones, and if I ever want to, say, relive the gonzo days of 2e using superior 3e rules as a base, I'd be fine with having such &quot;basic Daiklaves&quot; and counting them as 2-dots artifacts for the purpose of party craftsman churning them out so those armies of enlightened mortals and warghosts and whatnot had something to play with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T01:29:58-08:00","id":1369531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369530#post1369530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I acknowledged that in the very beginning. What I'm arguing is that this is due to a thematic choice of having each artifact weapon and armor a unique relic with unique magical powers, and not due to the overwhelming power of the artifact weapon/armor stats themselves, and that if one were to willfully and knowingly ignore that thematic restriction and allow an artifact whose sole power is having artifact weapon stats, it wouldn't be strong enough to merit a 3-dots cost, and thus would be more fairly priced as a 2-dot artifact.<br /> <br /> Which, again, I'm not saying everyone should allow such an item in their games. I'm all for Daiklaves being unique Zanpakutos. But there are different people, different campaigns and different tones, and if I ever want to, say, relive the gonzo days of 2e using superior 3e rules as a base, I'd be fine with having such &amp;quot;basic Daiklaves&amp;quot; and counting them as 2-dots artifacts for the purpose of party craftsman churning them out so those armies of enlightened mortals and warghosts and whatnot had something to play with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love 2E's Magitech Factory-Cathedral, Industrial Revolution with Magic theme. I like the idea of mass produced Artifacts.<br /> <br /> I disagree with your assessment.<br /> <br /> Just having the Artifact statline is worth 3 dots. Period.<br /> <br /> To have Evocations on top, you have to BUY those Evocations (either as Charms or with XP). Evocations are balanced by being an additional cost on top of the Artifact statline. <br /> <br /> That statline is what you pay 3 Merit dots for.<br /> <br /> Weapons and Armor with Artifact stats are absolutely worth three dots even if they have no other powers or potential. With no attunement bonus, no Hearthstone Slots and no Evocations, they're still worth more than 2 dots.<br /> <br /> Look at the published 2 dot Artifacts. An Artifact weapon is worth WAAAY more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T22:44:00-07:00","id":1393744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1369347#post1369347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the difference between a 3-dot artifact weapon and a 5-dot artifact weapon if you never take Evocations for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>the ability to fly the fact it comes with claws the same stat line as an artifact weapon... ability to breathe underwater","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T15:09:46-07:00","id":1393860,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't allow a goremaul for 2 dots. The difference between that a normal hammer feels too much for me and just saying it doesn't have evocations doesn't really work for me since a newly created artifact doesn't technically have evocations either and they have to be made at 3 dots. Maybe you could trade the extra dot for some kind of flaw to buy off, but that feels a bit too much like the old Dnd munchkin joke of &quot;Oh yeah I traded my ability to wink greater weapon strike.&quot; to me.<br /> <br /> Now I do like the idea of the hearthstone or magic item that creates/turns into a warhammer that sounds cool and decent enough I can see it working for the price","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T07:09:39-07:00","id":1394330,"title":"","content":"One of my threads was necro'd? I think I just gained a dot of Essence. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T06:03:09-07:00","id":1396004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1394330#post1394330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my threads was necro'd? I think I just gained a dot of Essence. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>4 months isn't much of a necro nowadays; you probably just got some Solar XP.<br /> <br /> :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T08:07:10-07:00","id":1396023,"title":"","content":"Here's my take now that the thread is 4 months old and the chance that my advice may be useful to the OP is close to zero. While artifact is clearly a story merit the cost of purchased merits is (new rating)*3. I think that it's balanced to put an xp hurdle in the way of them using the weapon as a goremaul. I'd be tempted to give the character and artifact 3 moonsilver goremaul with evocations based around the weapon changing shape. The &quot;goremaul&quot; is presently in the shape of a war hammer and the evocation to change it back into a proper goremaul is two or three deep in the tree, perhaps at an essence level higher then the PC starts at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 06-12-2020, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T09:29:03-07:00","id":1396033,"title":"","content":"Wouldn\u2019t it be easier just to sit down with the player to go through his character and see where he can shave off 1 measly point of freebies or merits to avoid all the headache and let him have an actual Goremaul ?<br /> p.s or let him start with xp debt if he has a good reason to start with one. If anything else it sounds like a player / communication issue than a rules issue since it\u2019s only 1 point to go up to artefact 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12796,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","user":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","date":". 06-12-2020, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T10:55:53-07:00","id":1396043,"title":"","content":"If this is somehow still unresolved from February then there's much bigger problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T04:31:47-07:00","id":1396153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368475-artifact-\u2022\u2022-goremaul?p=1394330#post1394330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my threads was necro'd? I think I just gained a dot of Essence. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Your thread was necro'd, but it was done by a person going &quot;um actually&quot; at what is literally the most recent time that other user made a post...<br /> <br /> From four months ago.<br /> <br /> Another person bringing up an old (defunct?) discussion to get a dig in at an echo might grant you a dot of Essence, but I find it takes a few hours off the end of my life.<br /> <br /> That sucks. I was gonna watch Shin Godzilla one last time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}